  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Dance-song of the Banyankole of southwestern Uganda, centred on Mbarara, whose stamping, arm-raising movements imitate the gait and horns of the long-horned cattle at the heart of Ankole herding life. Songs in praise of cattle alternate with okwevuga, rapid recited praise-poetry declaimed by the performers, and the dance is often accompanied by the endingidi tube fiddle.",
